  "raw_label": "appellant_lost",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Pankaj Dattatray Turekar vs The State Of Maharashtra on 30 January, 2024 Author: Sarang V. Kotwal Bench: Sarang V. Kotwal 2024:Bhc-As:5104 Gokhale 1 of 4 25-aba-3 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 3323 Of 2022 Darshan Dattatray Turekar ..Applic Versus State of Maharashtra ..Respon With Anticipatory Bail Application No. 3357 Of 2022 Pankaj Dattatray Turekar ..Applic Versus State of Maharashtra ..Respon ______ Mr. S. K. Ali a/w. Shabi Fatma a/w. Asif Ali a/w. Pratibha Gupta i/b. A. A. Siddiquie & Associates for Applicant. Ms. Mahalakshmi Ganapathy, App for State/Respondent. ___ _ _ _ Coram : Sarang V. Kotwal, J. Date : 30 January 2024 P.C. : 1.",
    "facts": "The police had intercepted a tempo bearing No.MH12/LT-1609 carrying banned food articles containing tobacco and pan masala. The tempo was searched and the banned food articles namely scented tobacco, pan masala etc. worth Rs.5,58,000/- were seized. Therefore, they are apprehending their arrest.",
    "arguments": "They are not connected with the arrested accused. He further submitted that, Section 328 of the I.P.C. is not attracted. Thus, the applicants have misused their liberty."
  },
